# open62541-qnx change: udp-empty-datagram
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
#
# title: Do not close a UDP socket because of an empty datagram
# file: open62541.c
# upstream: arch/eventloop_posix_udp.c
# test: pubsub.unicast.empty_datagram
#
# A UDP datagram without payload is a valid datagram, and recvfrom() returns
# 0 for it. The code takes every result <= 0 except EINTR as the end of the
# socket and closes it. A PubSub connection of this release does not reopen a
# receive socket that the EventLoop has closed: its connection callback
# reconnects only in the state Operational (src/pubsub/ua_pubsub_eventloop.c),
# and UA_PubSubConnection_setPubSubState() never stores that state for a
# connection, only PreOperational (src/pubsub/ua_pubsub_connection.c). One
# empty datagram leaves the subscriber without a socket, while its ReaderGroup
# and DataSetReader still report Operational. Anybody who can reach the port
# can send that datagram.
#
# The same branch also closes the socket after EAGAIN or EWOULDBLOCK, which say
# only that no datagram is waiting.
#
@@ hunk
